      <p class="top" id="en"><a href="/">← KERN</a> · <a href="#it" lang="it">Italiano</a> · <a href="#de" lang="de">Deutsch</a> · <a href="#fr" lang="fr">Français</a></p>
      <h1>About KERN</h1>
      <small>Don’t guess your passion. Test it.</small>
      <h2>What it is</h2>
      <p>KERN is a free app to find your passion by testing different paths. You try short missions in seven fields (design, writing, code, video, selling online, music and prompting with AI), say in 20 seconds how each one felt, and see which path clicks. No account needed.</p>
      <p>Seven creative and digital paths, for now.</p>
      <h2>Who makes it</h2>
      <p>KERN is made by Manuel Di Paolo, in Italy. Write to <a href="mailto:manuel@trykern.it">manuel@trykern.it</a> for anything: a question, feedback, or your data.</p>
      <h2>For parents</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><b>Age:</b> KERN is for people aged 18 and over for now, because it is built for adults and keeps what people write.</li>
        <li><b>What is stored:</b> without an account, answers, reflections and settings stay in the browser on that device. With an account, a copy is kept at Supabase in the EU (Frankfurt, Germany), so it syncs across devices.</li>
        <li><b>KERN.AI:</b> the co-pilot only asks questions. What someone types to it is sent to the AI provider (Anthropic) to get a reply, and KERN does not keep it. If a message sounds heavy, it pauses the mission and suggests talking to someone they trust or a local helpline.</li>
        <li><b>No ads:</b> no advertising and no cookies. Usage counts stay off unless the person says yes, and never include a name or anything they wrote.</li>
        <li><b>Nothing shared without consent:</b> no company sees an answer unless the person chooses to send it, one mission at a time. That is not active yet.</li>
        <li><b>Deleting:</b> in Settings, Delete my data (or Delete my account) removes everything. You can also write to <a href="mailto:manuel@trykern.it">manuel@trykern.it</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="foot"><a href="/privacy/">Privacy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms</a></p>
